It builds on work by others, whose licences it keeps:

  * ExTbpMonty.Core — the Thousand Brains Project's sensorimotor framework, ported
    to the BEAM (https://github.com/d-led/ex.tbp.monty), which is the project's
    own reimplementation of Monty (MIT, Copyright (c) Thousand Brains Project).
    This package calls its percept rather than re-implementing one.
  * ExQuiddity — quiddity and the exact B-rep under it, bound for the BEAM
    (https://github.com/d-led/ex.quiddity), MPL-2.0 for the binding and Apache
    License 2.0 for the engine (https://github.com/pzfreo/quiddity). Used as a
    dependency; not modified here.

The STEP test fixture under `test/fixtures/` came from quiddity's own test suite,
which takes it from public sources; each file names its source beside it.

The plate under `test/fixtures/solidcraft_sample_plate.step` is an unmodified
STEP export of SolidCraft's own sample plate.

  * SolidCraft — https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft — MIT OR Apache-2.0,
    Copyright (c) SolidCraft contributors. It is a parametric CAD modeller whose
    examples are JSON models (`examples/*.json`); the fixture is what
    `solidcraft-cli run <model>.json --out <part>.step` writes. The model is used
    as geometry only: nothing of SolidCraft is linked, copied or modified here.
